values ('ap_chemistry', 2, '2.1', array['2.1']::text[], 'convention', 'Classifying a bond as ionic or covalent', 'Metal–nonmetal bonds are generally ionic and nonmetal–nonmetal bonds are generally covalent, but electronegativity difference alone does not decide it, and the compound''s properties are the best way to characterize the bonding.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'All polar bonds have some ionic character, so ionic and covalent bonding form a continuum rather than two distinct categories.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-chemistry-reference-u2-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_chemistry-u2-r1-005; ced=2.1.A.4 "Examination of the properties of a compound is the best way to characterize the type of bonding"; 2.1.A.3.iii')
