values ('ap_chemistry', 2, '2.1', array['2.1', '2.7']::text[], 'convention', 'Direction and size of a bond dipole', 'In a polar bond the more electronegative atom takes the partial negative charge, and in single bonds a greater electronegativity difference gives a greater bond dipole.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-chemistry-reference-u2-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_chemistry-u2-r1-004; ced=2.1.A.3.i–ii "greater differences in electronegativity lead to greater bond dipoles"')
