values ('ap_chemistry', 2, '2.2', array['2.2']::text[], 'diagram', 'Potential energy vs. internuclear distance graph', 'Graph of potential energy versus the distance between two atoms, used to describe the interaction between the atoms, with the lowest-energy point marking the equilibrium bond length and the bond energy read from the energy needed to separate the atoms.', '[{"label": "Vertical axis: potential energy", "meaning": "Potential energy of the pair of interacting atoms."}, {"label": "Horizontal axis: internuclear distance", "meaning": "Distance between the nuclei of the two atoms."}, {"label": "Lowest point of the curve", "meaning": "Equilibrium bond length: the separation between atoms at which the potential energy is lowest."}, {"label": "Depth of the energy well", "meaning": "Bond energy: the energy required to separate the atoms."}, {"label": "Effect of bond order", "meaning": "Bonds with a higher order (single, double, triple) are shorter and have larger bond energies."}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-chemistry-reference-u2-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_chemistry-u2-r2-002; ced=2.2.A.1: "graph of potential energy versus the distance between atoms (internuclear distance)"; "equilibrium bond length (the separation between atoms at which the potential energy is lowest)"; "bond ')
