values ('ap_chemistry', 2, '2.4', array['2.4']::text[], 'diagram', 'Sea-of-electrons model of metallic bonding', 'A metallic solid is drawn as an array of positive metal ions surrounded by delocalized valence electrons.', '[{"label": "Positive metal ions", "meaning": "Cores of the metal atoms arranged in an array."}, {"label": "Delocalized valence electrons", "meaning": "The \"sea of electrons\" surrounding the ions, not tied to any one atom."}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-chemistry-reference-u2-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_chemistry-u2-r1-011; ced=2.4.A.1 "array of positive metal ions surrounded by delocalized valence electrons (i.e., a ''sea of electrons'')"')
