values ('ap_chemistry', 2, '2.6', array['2.6']::text[], 'formula', 'Formal charge of an atom in a Lewis diagram', '\text{FC} = (\text{valence e}^-\text{ of the free atom}) - (\text{nonbonding e}^-) - \tfrac{1}{2}(\text{bonding e}^-)', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'The CED does not print this formula; it requires students to calculate formal charges and use them to select among Lewis structures. Start from the correct number of valence electrons, since using the wrong number is a common mistake.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-chemistry-reference-u2-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_chemistry-u2-r2-005; ced=2.6.A.2 and Unit 2 ''Preparing for the AP Exam'': "calculating and connecting formal charges in Lewis structures"')
